    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nDisclaimer: This issue proposes specific solution to a problem that may have multiple possible solutions.\n\nI want to execute keys in a \"virtual\" buffer and get the resulting text and cursor position. The main problem is that we cannot set the cursor position for the buffer, only for the window. Setting the cursor for `vim._with` could allow dry-running user input against a hidden buffer.\n\nFor context, my main use case is mirroring user input from [mini.pick](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.pick) or [mini.input](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.input), which intercept user input and display it outside the buffer. I believe `mini.pick` displays user input as border text.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n```lua\nvim._with({ buf = 2, cursor = { 1, 0 } }, function()\n  --\nend)\n```",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
